# OKLCH Color Values

All color values MUST be specified using `oklch(...)` or transformed from an OKLCH source value.

## Required pattern

- Prefer explicit `oklch(...)` values for authored colors.
- If a target format is required by an external API, generator, editor theme format, or test fixture, derive it from an OKLCH source value in code.
- Keep the OKLCH source close to the transformed value so future edits preserve the intended color space.
- Do not introduce raw hex, RGB, HSL, named colors, or other color literals unless they are generated from OKLCH or required as non-authored fixture output.

```ts
// BAD: raw authored color literal
const accent = "#82aaff";

// GOOD: authored OKLCH source
const accent = "oklch(72% 0.14 260)";

// GOOD: external format derived from OKLCH
const accent = toHex("oklch(72% 0.14 260)");
```

When modifying existing colors, convert the source of truth to OKLCH first, then update any derived outputs or snapshots.
